// Team Banter Configuration
//
// What each team says when its kill-target call changes. Loaded and validated
// at GRAPHICAL startup only by BanterConfigPlugin
// (src/states/play_match/banter_config.rs); the plugin panics at startup if
// this file is missing, malformed, or fails validation.
//
// Unlike movement.ron, this file is NEVER read in headless mode — banter is
// visual-only, so a malformed pool can never stop a balance sweep and the
// content can never become a sim input.
//
// ===========================================================================
// COMBATANTS DO NOT SPEAK ENGLISH
// ===========================================================================
//
// A line is a short sequence of the game's OWN iconography — real ability art
// and team-framed class portraits — joined by drawn grammar marks.
// `{ability:Mortal Strike} {emoji:arrow} {target}` reads as "attack that one"
// without belonging to any language, in the visual vocabulary the player
// already learned from the ability bar.
//
// NO TYPESET EMOJI. egui's font atlas is a single coverage channel, so colour
// emoji are impossible here whatever font is loaded, and the monochrome
// fallbacks are not recognisable enough to carry meaning. Everything
// pictographic is therefore an IMAGE — real ability art, a class portrait, or
// an emoji PNG referenced by `{emoji:<filename stem>}` (see
// assets/icons/emoji/ATTRIBUTION.md). The only literal text permitted is
// punctuation.
//
// Tokens (see src/states/play_match/banter/vocab.rs for the grammar):
//
//   {target}                 portrait of the called enemy, framed by ITS team
//   {prev_target}            the replaced target's portrait (Correction only)
//   {speaker}                the speaking combatant's own portrait
//   {ability:Mortal Strike}  that ability's real icon art
//   {emoji:arrow}            art from assets/icons/emoji/arrow.png
//
// Portraits are FRAMED blue for team 1 and red for team 2 — the same colours
// the combat-log timeline uses. A frame rather than a tint: tinting multiplied
// the portrait's own colours and muddied the class silhouette.
//
// KNOWN LIMITATION: a portrait names a CLASS, not a combatant. A team fielding
// two of the same class renders the same portrait for both, so a line cannot
// distinguish them. Acceptable for now; the fix would be per-combatant marks.
//
// TEXT IS ALLOWLISTED to punctuation (`! ? … . , ·`) — these are ordinary font
// characters, not emoji, and `!` and `?` are about as universally read as a
// mark can be. Validation rejects anything else, naming the character, so an
// unrenderable or off-conceit line cannot reach a match.
//
// ABILITY ICONS NAME A CLASS THAT IS IN THE MATCH (rule settled 2026-09-13).
// An {ability:X} icon is a REFERENCE to a class party to the exchange — the
// speaker's own kit, a bound teammate's kit (asking a teammate to press one
// of THEIR buttons is a legitimate interaction; pushy types exist), or the
// called target's kit (naming the threat: "{ability:Flash Heal} {emoji:no}"
// = stop their healing). An icon whose class may be ABSENT from the match is
// confusing and forbidden — which rules out any specific class's ability as
// a generic verb in an Any-speaker line; intent is spoken in emoji verbs
// instead (sword/swords = attack, skull = kill intent, headstone = the
// resulting death, equals = "amounts to", no + ability = deny it).
// Operationally: presence is only GUARANTEED by the entry's own bindings, so
// an icon's class must appear among the entry's bound speaker classes or its
// target class. (A "class present anywhere in the match" resolver condition
// would be an engine extension — not built.)
//
// Vocabulary in play, and what each says in context. The VERBS are emoji —
// an ability icon is a class reference under the ownership rule above,
// never a verb:
//   {emoji:sword} {emoji:swords} attack / engage     {emoji:arrow}    directs at a target
//   {emoji:skull}                kill intent         {emoji:no}       no / stop / deny that
//   {emoji:headstone}            the resulting death {emoji:yes}      yes / on it
//   {emoji:equals}               "amounts to"        {emoji:thumbsup} casual ack
//   {emoji:bandage}              healing, a healer   {emoji:eyes}     watch for it
//   {emoji:seenoevil}            cannot see it       {emoji:speaknoevil} shut up
//   {emoji:thinking}             hesitation          !  ?  …          urgency / doubt / waiting
//
// PICK EMOJI THAT ARE ACTUALLY COLOURFUL. Several Unicode dingbats render in
// Twemoji as near-greyscale — ✔️ is dark slate, 🔍 is grey — and at 20px in a
// moving bubble they read as smudges next to the saturated ability art. The
// colourful sibling usually exists and says the same thing: ✅ for the check,
// 🙈 for "I cannot see it". Check the PNG before adding a token, not after.
//
// ===========================================================================
// HOW THE POOL IS TIERED
// ===========================================================================
//
// Coverage is total from day one and deepens by appending, never by filling a
// grid. Four tiers, loosest first:
//
//   1. generic       — any speaker, any target. The floor; always satisfiable.
//   2. by target     — the called class has a specific threat worth naming.
//   3. by speaker    — the caller's own kit colours the line.
//   4. full pair     — speaker AND target, only where a real joke exists.
//
// The resolver WEIGHTS by specificity (specificity_weight per non-Any
// constraint) rather than filtering, so a bespoke line lands often without
// ever crowding the generics out. Adding one is one appended entry.
//
// FALLBACK RULE (2026-09-14): when a slot resists tuning — a joke that has
// failed review twice, or interactive banter (Corrections and Switches,
// where a target swap must read INSTANTLY) — stop iterating and take the
// simple template instead: the plain call-and-ack shape the tier-1 generics
// and the signature-ability tier-3 entries use. A slot may also simply stay
// empty; the generics always cover it. Simplistic and legible beats clever
// and tuned-forever.
//
// SILENCE IN 1v1 IS DELIBERATE, AND THE ROLE COUNT ENFORCES IT.
// Every exchange — including the single-beat Switch shouts — declares two
// distinct speaker roles. A solo combatant cannot bind both, so nothing is
// satisfiable and a 1v1 team says nothing, in the countdown AND mid-fight.
// The Switch entries get a silent "witness" role with no beat: someone has to
// be there to hear it.
(
    timing: (
        // ---- PACING -------------------------------------------------------
        // The whole tuning surface for how banter reads. Re-read at startup,
        // so tuning is edit-and-relaunch with no rebuild. If lines feel
        // rushed, raise `line_lifetime` first and `beat_gap` second.
        //
        // Two bounds constrain it. `latest_beat` bounds how late an exchange's
        // last beat may speak; spilling past the 10s countdown is allowed and
        // deliberate (see `latest_beat` below). And validation rejects a pool
        // where `line_lifetime` minus a context's start delay reaches its beat
        // gap — a floor on how tightly beats may be spaced. That formula is
        // inherited from a mechanism the scheduler no longer has;
        // `banter_config.rs` says so at the check itself rather than
        // inventing a tidier reason for it.

        // Seconds after the call change before the first beat speaks. Applies
        // to Opening and Correction, both of which play during the countdown
        // while combatants are still settling into the starting room.
        opening_start: 1.5,
        // A mid-fight Switch shout does NOT wait that out — its job is to make
        // the operator's order legible the moment it is given.
        switch_start: 0.8,
        // Seconds between consecutive beats (Opening and Switch). Below
        // `line_lifetime` on purpose: consecutive lines overlap a little so an
        // exchange reads as conversation rather than as a slideshow.
        // At 2.5 an Opening exchange fits FIVE beats (1.5 / 4.0 / 6.5 / 9.0 /
        // 11.5 against latest_beat 12.0) — four inside the countdown, and the
        // fifth spilling into the opening approach (see latest_beat).
        //
        // THIS KNOB IS FENCED ON BOTH SIDES, and the ceiling is the tight one:
        // the longest Opening exchange has five beats, so its last starts at
        // `opening_start + 4 * beat_gap` and must not pass `latest_beat`.
        // That caps beat_gap at 2.625 — only 0.125 above the shipped value.
        // The floor is 1.7, from the spacing check at `line_lifetime`. Safe
        // range (1.7, 2.625]; measured, not derived — 2.625 validates and
        // 2.63 fails with "beat 4 starts at 12.02s, past timing.latest_beat".
        // Raising this wants `latest_beat` raised with it.
        beat_gap: 2.5,
        // How long each bubble stays up — the read-time knob. A speaker who
        // starts a new line while their last is still up REPLACES it, so
        // consecutive beats on ONE role are allowed and read as that speaker
        // talking over themselves. The first line's screen time is cut to the
        // beat gap; that shortening is the overcommunication, not a defect.
        //
        // Bounded above at 3.9. Validation requires `line_lifetime` minus a
        // context's start delay to stay BELOW that context's beat gap, and it
        // checks only contexts that actually hold a multi-beat exchange. Two
        // qualify: Opening (3.2 - 1.5 = 1.7 against beat_gap 2.5) and
        // Correction (1.7 against correction_beat_gap 2.4). Correction has
        // the smaller gap, so it binds first — 3.8 validates, 3.9 fails
        // naming Correction. Switch is NOT checked: all its entries are
        // single-beat shouts, so it has no interval to constrain. Authoring a
        // two-beat Switch would turn its row on and tighten the ceiling to
        // `switch_start + beat_gap`.
        //
        // The formula is inherited from a mechanism the scheduler no longer
        // has — `banter_config.rs` gives the honest account of what it does
        // and does not measure, at the check itself.
        line_lifetime: 3.2,
        // Tighter pacing for corrections — they race the gates. Floor 1.7,
        // the same spacing check: 1.8 validates, 1.7 fails. No ceiling worth
        // naming — the longest Correction runs three beats.
        correction_beat_gap: 2.4,
        // The countdown is 10s, but a conversation MAY spill past the gates
        // (ruling 2026-09-14): the walk across the arena's dead space —
        // Nagrand especially — leaves ample time to finish talking before
        // contact, and the scheduler already plays late beats. This bounds
        // the tail so an exchange still ends well before combat closes.
        //
        // It cannot drop below 11.5 at the shipped beat_gap: the five-beat
        // Opening exchange puts its last beat at 11.5s, and a beat starting
        // past this value fails validation. Measured — 11.5 validates, 11.4
        // fails. Lowering this means lowering `beat_gap` first.
        latest_beat: 12.0,
        // Selection-weight multiplier per non-Any constraint. 1.0 would make
        // specificity irrelevant; this favours a bespoke exchange without
        // ever crowding the generics out.
        specificity_weight: 3.0,
    ),
    exchanges: [
        // =====================================================================
        // OPENING — the countdown exchange
        // =====================================================================

        // ---- tier 1: generic ------------------------------------------------
        (
            context: Opening,
            speakers: [ (role: "caller", class: Any), (role: "responder", class: Any) ],
            target: Any,
            beats: [
                (role: "caller",    text: "{emoji:sword} {target} {emoji:arrow} {emoji:skull}"),
                (role: "responder", text: "{emoji:yes}"),
            ],
        ),
        (
            context: Opening,
            speakers: [ (role: "caller", class: Any), (role: "responder", class: Any) ],
            target: Any,
            beats: [
                (role: "caller",    text: "..."),
                (role: "responder", text: "..."),
                (role: "caller",    text: "{emoji:thinking}"),
                (role: "caller",    text: "{target} ?"),
                (role: "responder", text: "{target} !"),
            ],
        ),
        (
            context: Opening,
            speakers: [ (role: "caller", class: Any), (role: "responder", class: Any) ],
            target: Any,
            beats: [
                (role: "caller",    text: "{emoji:skull} {emoji:arrow} {target}"),
                (role: "responder", text: "{emoji:no} {target}"),
                (role: "responder", text: "{emoji:math} {emoji:arrow} {emoji:test_tube} {emoji:arrow} {emoji:lightbulb} {emoji:arrow} {emoji:book}"),
                (role: "caller",    text: "{emoji:speaknoevil} ! {emoji:skull} {emoji:arrow} {target} !"),
            ],
        ),

        // ---- tier 2: by target ----------------------------------------------
        // The healer dies first, and everyone knows why.
        (
            context: Opening,
            speakers: [ (role: "caller", class: Any), (role: "responder", class: Any) ],
            target: Class(Priest),
            beats: [
                (role: "caller",    text: "{target} {ability:Flash Heal} {emoji:no}"),
                (role: "responder", text: "{emoji:skull} {emoji:arrow} {target} {emoji:equals} {emoji:headstone} !"),
            ],
        ),
        (
            context: Opening,
            speakers: [ (role: "caller", class: Any), (role: "responder", class: Any) ],
            target: Class(Paladin),
            beats: [
                (role: "caller",    text: "{target} {ability:Flash of Light} {emoji:no}"),
                (role: "responder", text: "{emoji:skull} {emoji:arrow} {target} {emoji:equals} {emoji:headstone} !"),
            ],
        ),
        (
            context: Opening,
            speakers: [ (role: "caller", class: Any), (role: "responder", class: Any) ],
            target: Class(Shaman),
            beats: [
                (role: "caller",    text: "{target} {ability:Lesser Healing Wave} {emoji:no}"),
                (role: "responder", text: "{emoji:skull} {emoji:arrow} {target} {emoji:equals} {emoji:headstone} !"),
            ],
        ),
        (
            context: Opening,
            speakers: [ (role: "caller", class: Any), (role: "responder", class: Any) ],
            target: Class(Rogue),
            beats: [
                (role: "caller",    text: "{emoji:ninja} {emoji:equals} {emoji:angry}"),
                (role: "responder", text: "{emoji:swords} {target} ?"),
                (role: "caller",    text: "{emoji:thumbsup} {emoji:thumbsup} {emoji:thumbsup}"),
            ],
        ),
        (
            context: Opening,
            speakers: [ (role: "caller", class: Any), (role: "responder", class: Any) ],
            target: Class(Mage),
            beats: [
                (role: "caller",    text: "{emoji:no} {ability:Polymorph}"),
                (role: "responder", text: "{emoji:thumbsup}"),
                (role: "responder", text: "{emoji:swords} {target}?"),
                (role: "caller",    text: "{emoji:thumbsup}"),
            ],
        ),
        (
            context: Opening,
            speakers: [ (role: "caller", class: Any), (role: "responder", class: Any) ],
            target: Class(Warlock),
            beats: [
                (role: "caller",    text: "{emoji:no} {ability:Fear}"),
                (role: "responder", text: "{emoji:thumbsup}"),
                (role: "responder", text: "{emoji:swords} {target}?"),
                (role: "caller",    text: "{emoji:thumbsup}"),
            ],
        ),
        (
            context: Opening,
            speakers: [ (role: "caller", class: Any), (role: "responder", class: Any) ],
            target: Class(Warrior),
            beats: [
                (role: "caller",    text: "{emoji:sword} {emoji:monkey} {target}"),
                (role: "responder", text: "{emoji:monkey} {emoji:banana} {emoji:monkey} {emoji:banana} {emoji:yes}!"),
            ],
        ),
        // The footrace dread — a Hunter kill means Disengage, then running,
        // and running. Flat periods; the resignation is the joke.
        (
            context: Opening,
            speakers: [ (role: "caller", class: Any), (role: "responder", class: Any) ],
            target: Class(Hunter),
            beats: [
                (role: "caller",    text: "{emoji:skull} {emoji:arrow} {target} ."),
                (role: "responder", text: "{target} {emoji:equals} {ability:Disengage} {emoji:run} {emoji:run} …"),
                (role: "caller",    text: "{emoji:run} {emoji:yes} . {emoji:skull} {emoji:yes} ."),
            ],
        ),

        // ---- tier 3: by speaker ---------------------------------------------
        (
            context: Opening,
            speakers: [ (role: "caller", class: Class(Rogue)), (role: "responder", class: Any) ],
            target: Any,
            beats: [
                (role: "caller",    text: "{ability:Ambush} {emoji:arrow} {target}"),
                (role: "responder", text: "{emoji:seenoevil} …"),
            ],
        ),
        (
            context: Opening,
            speakers: [ (role: "caller", class: Class(Warrior)), (role: "responder", class: Any) ],
            target: Any,
            beats: [
                (role: "caller",    text: "{ability:Charge} {emoji:arrow} {target}"),
                (role: "responder", text: "!"),
            ],
        ),
        (
            context: Opening,
            speakers: [ (role: "caller", class: Any), (role: "responder", class: Class(Priest)) ],
            target: Any,
            beats: [
                (role: "caller",    text: "{emoji:sword} {emoji:arrow} {target} {ability:Flash Heal} ?"),
                (role: "responder", text: "{ability:Flash Heal} {emoji:yes}"),
            ],
        ),
        (
            context: Opening,
            speakers: [ (role: "caller", class: Any), (role: "responder", class: Class(Paladin)) ],
            target: Any,
            beats: [
                (role: "caller",    text: "{emoji:sword} {emoji:arrow} {target} !"),
                (role: "responder", text: "{ability:Flash of Light} {emoji:yes}"),
            ],
        ),
        // The escape drill: "and when melee closes?" — "Disengage. Trap.
        // Run." (verbatim the AI's dead-zone priority ladder; the flat
        // periods are the fire-drill cadence).
        (
            context: Opening,
            speakers: [ (role: "caller", class: Class(Hunter)), (role: "responder", class: Any) ],
            target: Any,
            beats: [
                (role: "caller",    text: "{ability:Aimed Shot} {emoji:arrow} {target}"),
                (role: "responder", text: "{emoji:swords} {emoji:dash} ?"),
                (role: "caller",    text: "{ability:Disengage} . {ability:Frost Trap} . {emoji:run} ."),
                (role: "responder", text: "{emoji:thumbsup} …"),
            ],
        ),
        (
            context: Opening,
            speakers: [ (role: "caller", class: Class(Warlock)), (role: "responder", class: Any) ],
            target: Any,
            beats: [
                (role: "caller",    text: "{ability:Corruption} {emoji:arrow} {target}"),
                (role: "responder", text: "… {emoji:yes}"),
            ],
        ),
        (
            context: Opening,
            speakers: [ (role: "caller", class: Class(Mage)), (role: "responder", class: Any) ],
            target: Any,
            beats: [
                (role: "caller",    text: "{ability:Frost Nova} {emoji:arrow} {target}"),
                (role: "responder", text: "{emoji:yes}"),
            ],
        ),
        (
            context: Opening,
            speakers: [ (role: "caller", class: Class(Shaman)), (role: "responder", class: Any) ],
            target: Any,
            beats: [
                (role: "caller",    text: "{ability:Lightning Bolt} {emoji:arrow} {target}"),
                (role: "responder", text: "{emoji:yes}"),
            ],
        ),

        // Paladin caller — the SIMPLE sibling template, deliberately: two
        // joke rounds failed review here, and the fallback rule (see the
        // tiering header) says stop tuning and take the plain form.
        (
            context: Opening,
            speakers: [ (role: "caller", class: Class(Paladin)), (role: "responder", class: Any) ],
            target: Any,
            beats: [
                (role: "caller",    text: "{ability:Hammer of Justice} {emoji:arrow} {target}"),
                (role: "responder", text: "{emoji:yes}"),
            ],
        ),
        // The Light told me who dies (responder sarcasm per review tweak).
        (
            context: Opening,
            speakers: [ (role: "caller", class: Class(Priest)), (role: "responder", class: Any) ],
            target: Any,
            beats: [
                (role: "caller",    text: "{emoji:pray} …"),
                (role: "caller",    text: "{emoji:sparkles} ! {emoji:skull} {emoji:arrow} {target}"),
                (role: "responder", text: "… {emoji:pray} ? {emoji:shrug} {emoji:yes}"),
            ],
        ),
        // The aggressive Priest: "and who heals ME?" — "the Light will
        // provide." (Mechanically true: the AI only Mind Blasts while its
        // allies are healthy.)
        (
            context: Opening,
            speakers: [ (role: "caller", class: Class(Priest)), (role: "responder", class: Any) ],
            target: Any,
            beats: [
                (role: "caller",    text: "{ability:Mind Blast} {emoji:arrow} {target} !"),
                (role: "responder", text: "{ability:Flash Heal} {emoji:arrow} {speaker} … ?"),
                (role: "caller",    text: "{emoji:pray} {emoji:sparkles}"),
            ],
        ),
        // Every answer is Charge.
        (
            context: Opening,
            speakers: [ (role: "caller", class: Any), (role: "responder", class: Class(Warrior)) ],
            target: Any,
            beats: [
                (role: "caller",    text: "{emoji:thinking} {target} ?"),
                (role: "responder", text: "{ability:Charge}"),
                (role: "caller",    text: "{emoji:thinking} … {emoji:shield} ?"),
                (role: "responder", text: "{ability:Charge} !"),
            ],
        ),
        // The detailed plan nobody asked for — and it is CORRECT (the AI
        // really Polymorphs the non-kill target to make the 2v1).
        (
            context: Opening,
            speakers: [ (role: "caller", class: Any), (role: "responder", class: Class(Mage)) ],
            target: Any,
            beats: [
                (role: "caller",    text: "{emoji:sword} {emoji:arrow} {target} ?"),
                (role: "responder", text: "{ability:Polymorph} {emoji:arrow} {emoji:no} {target} , {ability:Frostbolt} {emoji:arrow} {target} , {ability:Frostbolt} ."),
                (role: "responder", text: "{emoji:stopwatch} {emoji:equals} {emoji:math} !"),
                (role: "caller",    text: "… {emoji:thumbsup}"),
            ],
        ),
        // The overplanning Rogue, dithering between its AI's two REAL chains.
        (
            context: Opening,
            speakers: [ (role: "caller", class: Any), (role: "responder", class: Class(Rogue)) ],
            target: Any,
            beats: [
                (role: "caller",    text: "{emoji:skull} {emoji:arrow} {target}"),
                (role: "responder", text: "{emoji:math} {ability:Cheap Shot} {emoji:arrow} {ability:Kidney Shot} {emoji:equals} {emoji:hourglass} {emoji:hourglass}"),
                (role: "responder", text: "{emoji:no} … {emoji:math} {ability:Kick} {emoji:arrow} … {emoji:arrow} {ability:Kidney Shot} ?"),
                (role: "caller",    text: "{emoji:interrobang}"),
            ],
        ),
        // The chill Rogue. It's all good. They'll figure it out out there.
        (
            context: Opening,
            speakers: [ (role: "caller", class: Any), (role: "responder", class: Class(Rogue)) ],
            target: Any,
            beats: [
                (role: "caller",    text: "{emoji:skull} {emoji:arrow} {target} ! {emoji:alert} !"),
                (role: "responder", text: "{emoji:surf}"),
                (role: "caller",    text: "? ? {emoji:target} ?"),
                (role: "responder", text: "{emoji:smirk} {emoji:thumbsup}"),
            ],
        ),
        // Surgical strike vs. arson ("fire? where did that come from!?" per
        // review tweak).
        (
            context: Opening,
            speakers: [ (role: "caller", class: Any), (role: "responder", class: Class(Warlock)) ],
            target: Any,
            beats: [
                (role: "caller",    text: "{emoji:skull} {emoji:arrow} {target} ?"),
                (role: "responder", text: "{emoji:imp} {emoji:yes} … {emoji:fire} {emoji:fire} {emoji:fire}"),
                (role: "caller",    text: "{emoji:fire} {emoji:fire} {emoji:fire} ! ?"),
                (role: "responder", text: "… {emoji:imp} {emoji:fire}"),
            ],
        ),
        // Furniture first, then the doctrine (the AI's literal priority 1 is
        // totem maintenance).
        (
            context: Opening,
            speakers: [ (role: "caller", class: Any), (role: "responder", class: Class(Shaman)) ],
            target: Any,
            beats: [
                (role: "caller",    text: "{emoji:skull} {emoji:arrow} {target} ?"),
                (role: "responder", text: "{ability:Windfury Totem} {ability:Healing Stream Totem} {ability:Strength of Earth Totem} {ability:Flametongue Totem} ."),
                (role: "responder", text: "{ability:Wind Shear} {emoji:equals} {emoji:speaknoevil} , {ability:Lightning Bolt} {emoji:arrow} {emoji:boom} !"),
                (role: "caller",    text: "… {emoji:thumbsup}"),
            ],
        ),

        // ---- tier 4: full pairs ---------------------------------------------
        // A Rogue promising to open on a healer, and the healer's own class
        // knowing exactly how that goes.
        (
            context: Opening,
            speakers: [ (role: "caller", class: Class(Rogue)), (role: "responder", class: Any) ],
            target: Class(Priest),
            beats: [
                (role: "caller",    text: "{ability:Cheap Shot} {emoji:arrow} {target}"),
                (role: "responder", text: "{target} {ability:Flash Heal} {emoji:no} !"),
            ],
        ),
        (
            context: Opening,
            speakers: [ (role: "caller", class: Class(Mage)), (role: "responder", class: Any) ],
            target: Class(Warrior),
            beats: [
                (role: "caller",    text: "{ability:Frost Nova} {emoji:arrow} {target} !"),
                (role: "responder", text: "{ability:Berserker Rage} ! …"),
            ],
        ),
        (
            context: Opening,
            speakers: [ (role: "caller", class: Class(Warrior)), (role: "responder", class: Any) ],
            target: Class(Mage),
            beats: [
                (role: "caller",    text: "{ability:Charge} {emoji:arrow} {target} {emoji:skull}"),
                (role: "responder", text: "{ability:Ice Barrier} ! ?"),
            ],
        ),
        (
            context: Opening,
            speakers: [ (role: "caller", class: Class(Priest)), (role: "responder", class: Any) ],
            target: Class(Paladin),
            beats: [
                (role: "caller",    text: "{speaker} {ability:Flash Heal} {emoji:sword} {target} {ability:Flash Heal}"),
                (role: "responder", text: "… … …"),
            ],
        ),

        // The plan meets the ranged interrupt.
        (
            context: Opening,
            speakers: [ (role: "caller", class: Class(Mage)), (role: "responder", class: Any) ],
            target: Class(Shaman),
            beats: [
                (role: "caller",    text: "{ability:Frostbolt} , {ability:Polymorph} , {ability:Frostbolt} ."),
                (role: "responder", text: "{target} {ability:Wind Shear} ?"),
                (role: "caller",    text: "… {emoji:angry} {emoji:angry} {emoji:angry}"),
                (role: "responder", text: "{emoji:skull} {emoji:arrow} {target} {emoji:equals} {emoji:headstone} !"),
            ],
        ),
        // Ban the bubble ("sure thing, monkey").
        (
            context: Opening,
            speakers: [ (role: "caller", class: Class(Warrior)), (role: "responder", class: Any) ],
            target: Class(Paladin),
            beats: [
                (role: "caller",    text: "{ability:Charge} {emoji:arrow} {target} !"),
                (role: "responder", text: "{target} {ability:Divine Shield} …"),
                (role: "caller",    text: "{emoji:angry} ! {ability:Divine Shield} {emoji:equals} {emoji:banned} !"),
                (role: "responder", text: "{emoji:monkey} {emoji:yes} {emoji:yes}"),
            ],
        ),
        // The snail. "you are a snail." (period.)
        (
            context: Opening,
            speakers: [ (role: "caller", class: Class(Warrior)), (role: "responder", class: Any) ],
            target: Class(Hunter),
            beats: [
                (role: "caller",    text: "{ability:Charge} {emoji:arrow} {target} !"),
                (role: "responder", text: "{target} {ability:Concussive Shot} … {emoji:snail}"),
                (role: "caller",    text: "{emoji:snail} {emoji:no} ! {emoji:muscle} !"),
                (role: "responder", text: "{emoji:snail} {emoji:yes} ."),
            ],
        ),
        // Evil is patient: the AI never Fears its own dotted kill target —
        // the rot IS the clock. ("no Fear" clause trimmed per review.)
        (
            context: Opening,
            speakers: [ (role: "caller", class: Class(Warlock)), (role: "responder", class: Any) ],
            target: Class(Priest),
            beats: [
                (role: "caller",    text: "{ability:Corruption} {emoji:arrow} {target} , {emoji:imp} {emoji:smirk}"),
                (role: "responder", text: "{target} {ability:Flash Heal} {emoji:no} ! {ability:Fear} ?"),
                (role: "caller",    text: "{ability:Corruption} {emoji:equals} {emoji:hourglass} {emoji:headstone} ."),
                (role: "responder", text: "{emoji:hourglass} {emoji:angry} …"),
            ],
        ),
        // "Dispel Psychic Scream and we win!" — a Priest speaker makes
        // Dispel Magic first-person-legal.
        (
            context: Opening,
            speakers: [ (role: "caller", class: Class(Priest)), (role: "responder", class: Any) ],
            target: Class(Priest),
            beats: [
                (role: "caller",    text: "{target} {ability:Psychic Scream} ? {ability:Dispel Magic} {emoji:equals} {emoji:trophy} !"),
                (role: "responder", text: "{emoji:scream} … {emoji:thumbsup}"),
            ],
        ),
        // Do not say the word.
        (
            context: Opening,
            speakers: [ (role: "caller", class: Class(Warrior)), (role: "responder", class: Any) ],
            target: Class(Mage),
            beats: [
                (role: "caller",    text: "{ability:Charge} {emoji:arrow} {target} !"),
                (role: "responder", text: "{ability:Frost Nova} ?"),
                (role: "caller",    text: "{emoji:speaknoevil} ! {emoji:angry} !"),
                (role: "responder", text: "{emoji:snowflake} …"),
            ],
        ),

        // =====================================================================
        // CORRECTION — the call changed before the gates
        // =====================================================================

        // ---- tier 1: generic ------------------------------------------------
        (
            context: Correction,
            speakers: [ (role: "caller", class: Any), (role: "responder", class: Any) ],
            target: Any,
            beats: [
                (role: "caller",    text: "{emoji:no} {prev_target} {emoji:arrow} {target}"),
                (role: "responder", text: "{emoji:yes}"),
            ],
        ),
        (
            context: Correction,
            speakers: [ (role: "caller", class: Any), (role: "responder", class: Any) ],
            target: Any,
            beats: [
                (role: "caller",    text: "{emoji:no} ! {target}"),
                (role: "responder", text: "{prev_target} ?"),
                (role: "caller",    text: "{target} !"),
            ],
        ),
        (
            context: Correction,
            speakers: [ (role: "caller", class: Any), (role: "responder", class: Any) ],
            target: Any,
            beats: [
                (role: "caller",    text: "{target} {emoji:swords}"),
                (role: "responder", text: "… {prev_target} ? ?!"),
            ],
        ),
        (
            context: Correction,
            speakers: [ (role: "caller", class: Any), (role: "responder", class: Any) ],
            target: Any,
            beats: [
                (role: "caller",    text: "{emoji:no} {emoji:no} {target} !"),
                (role: "responder", text: "… {emoji:no} {emoji:yes}"),
            ],
        ),
        // Simple retarget ack, from review: "them = dead", any target.
        (
            context: Correction,
            speakers: [ (role: "caller", class: Any), (role: "responder", class: Any) ],
            target: Any,
            beats: [
                (role: "caller",    text: "{emoji:no} {prev_target} {emoji:arrow} {target}"),
                (role: "responder", text: "{target} {emoji:equals} {emoji:skull}"),
            ],
        ),

        // ---- tier 2: by target ----------------------------------------------
        (
            context: Correction,
            speakers: [ (role: "caller", class: Any), (role: "responder", class: Any) ],
            target: Class(Priest),
            beats: [
                (role: "caller",    text: "{emoji:no} {prev_target} {emoji:arrow} {target} {ability:Flash Heal}"),
                (role: "responder", text: "! {emoji:yes}"),
            ],
        ),
        (
            context: Correction,
            speakers: [ (role: "caller", class: Any), (role: "responder", class: Any) ],
            target: Class(Rogue),
            beats: [
                (role: "caller",    text: "? ! {target}"),
                (role: "responder", text: "{emoji:seenoevil} ?"),
                (role: "caller",    text: "…"),
            ],
        ),

        // Plan around the abomination: the bubble runs out, then they die.
        (
            context: Correction,
            speakers: [ (role: "caller", class: Any), (role: "responder", class: Any) ],
            target: Class(Paladin),
            beats: [
                (role: "caller",    text: "{emoji:no} {prev_target} {emoji:arrow} {target} !"),
                (role: "responder", text: "{target} {ability:Divine Shield} … {emoji:angry}"),
                (role: "caller",    text: "{ability:Divine Shield} {emoji:arrow} {emoji:hourglass} , {emoji:skull} !"),
            ],
        ),
        // The lightning is already free.
        (
            context: Correction,
            speakers: [ (role: "caller", class: Any), (role: "responder", class: Any) ],
            target: Class(Shaman),
            beats: [
                (role: "caller",    text: "{emoji:no} {prev_target} ! {target} {ability:Lightning Bolt} !"),
                (role: "responder", text: "{emoji:zap} {emoji:zap} {emoji:zap} {emoji:scream}"),
                (role: "caller",    text: "{emoji:skull} {emoji:arrow} {target} !"),
            ],
        ),

        // One groan, then compliance.
        (
            context: Correction,
            speakers: [ (role: "caller", class: Any), (role: "responder", class: Any) ],
            target: Class(Mage),
            beats: [
                (role: "caller",    text: "{emoji:no} {prev_target} {emoji:arrow} {target} !"),
                (role: "responder", text: "{emoji:angry} {ability:Polymorph} … {emoji:yes}"),
            ],
        ),
        // The only delighted responder in the correction family.
        (
            context: Correction,
            speakers: [ (role: "caller", class: Any), (role: "responder", class: Any) ],
            target: Class(Warlock),
            beats: [
                (role: "caller",    text: "{emoji:no} {prev_target} {emoji:arrow} {target} !"),
                (role: "responder", text: "{ability:Fear} {emoji:angry} ! {emoji:yes} !"),
            ],
        ),
        // Weary acceptance of the footrace.
        (
            context: Correction,
            speakers: [ (role: "caller", class: Any), (role: "responder", class: Any) ],
            target: Class(Hunter),
            beats: [
                (role: "caller",    text: "{emoji:no} {prev_target} {emoji:arrow} {target}"),
                (role: "responder", text: "… {emoji:run} {emoji:yes}"),
            ],
        ),
        // (No Warrior-target Correction by decision — the generics cover it.)

        // =====================================================================
        // SWITCH — the call changed after the gates
        //
        // One spoken beat (R8), but TWO declared roles: the silent "witness"
        // has no line and exists solely so a solo combatant cannot satisfy the
        // exchange. That is what keeps 1v1 quiet mid-fight.
        // =====================================================================

        // ---- tier 1: generic ------------------------------------------------
        (
            context: Switch,
            speakers: [ (role: "caller", class: Any), (role: "witness", class: Any) ],
            target: Any,
            beats: [ (role: "caller", text: "! {emoji:arrow} {target}") ],
        ),
        (
            context: Switch,
            speakers: [ (role: "caller", class: Any), (role: "witness", class: Any) ],
            target: Any,
            beats: [ (role: "caller", text: "{emoji:swords} {target} !") ],
        ),
        (
            context: Switch,
            speakers: [ (role: "caller", class: Any), (role: "witness", class: Any) ],
            target: Any,
            beats: [ (role: "caller", text: "{target} {emoji:arrow} {emoji:skull} !") ],
        ),
        (
            context: Switch,
            speakers: [ (role: "caller", class: Any), (role: "witness", class: Any) ],
            target: Any,
            beats: [ (role: "caller", text: "{emoji:no} {emoji:arrow} {target}") ],
        ),

        // ---- tier 2: by target ----------------------------------------------
        (
            context: Switch,
            speakers: [ (role: "caller", class: Any), (role: "witness", class: Any) ],
            target: Class(Priest),
            beats: [ (role: "caller", text: "{target} {ability:Flash Heal} {emoji:no} !") ],
        ),
        (
            context: Switch,
            speakers: [ (role: "caller", class: Any), (role: "witness", class: Any) ],
            target: Class(Mage),
            beats: [ (role: "caller", text: "{target} {emoji:eyes} ! {emoji:swords}") ],
        ),
        (
            context: Switch,
            speakers: [ (role: "caller", class: Any), (role: "witness", class: Any) ],
            target: Class(Rogue),
            beats: [ (role: "caller", text: "? ! {target}") ],
        ),
        // The stop-their-signature-ability shout family (parallels Priest).
        (
            context: Switch,
            speakers: [ (role: "caller", class: Any), (role: "witness", class: Any) ],
            target: Class(Shaman),
            beats: [ (role: "caller", text: "{target} {ability:Lightning Bolt} {emoji:no} !") ],
        ),
        (
            context: Switch,
            speakers: [ (role: "caller", class: Any), (role: "witness", class: Any) ],
            target: Class(Warlock),
            beats: [ (role: "caller", text: "{target} ! {ability:Fear} {emoji:eyes} !") ],
        ),
        (
            context: Switch,
            speakers: [ (role: "caller", class: Any), (role: "witness", class: Any) ],
            target: Class(Warrior),
            beats: [ (role: "caller", text: "{emoji:monkey} ! {emoji:skull} {emoji:arrow} {target} !") ],
        ),
        (
            context: Switch,
            speakers: [ (role: "caller", class: Any), (role: "witness", class: Any) ],
            target: Class(Hunter),
            beats: [ (role: "caller", text: "{target} {emoji:run} {emoji:no} !") ],
        ),
        // "The bubble is just an hourglass!" — mechanically true rally cry.
        (
            context: Switch,
            speakers: [ (role: "caller", class: Any), (role: "witness", class: Any) ],
            target: Class(Paladin),
            beats: [ (role: "caller", text: "{target} {ability:Divine Shield} {emoji:equals} {emoji:hourglass} !") ],
        ),
    ],
)
